{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And it shall be, when you draw near to the battle.</b> Once they reach the border, all these conditions are stated to them. And one need not say 'if you draw near to battle,' for 'draw near' is written after it — 'Hear, O Israel, you draw near today' etc." "<b>And the priest shall approach and speak to the people.</b> A Tanna taught one thing: the priest speaks and the priest makes heard; and another Tanna taught: the officer speaks and the officer makes heard. Abaye said: from 'approach' until 'and they shall speak' — the priest speaks and the officer makes heard; from 'and they shall be added' onward — the officer speaks and the officer makes heard."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:27.537386471Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}